														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4823347">
									

<p>Hey! I posted this one before, but that was well over two weeks ago and it didn't get any responses. Figured I might as well try this forum again before looking into other critique options :) (I have made some very slight modifications since, anyway).</p>
<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout:</strong> Pretty standard SCP article layout, but I’m going to make heavy use of drop-down “click to reveal” sections to help break down the length.</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> SCP-XXXX is a 1&#160;m<sup>3</sup> metal safe that cannot be opened or damaged by any apparent means. It causes auditory hallucinations in those who stand within 10&#160;m of it for more than 3 hours (cumulative) that tempt them to try to open it. Eventually these victims convert into anomalous humanoids with an innate knowledge of SCP-XXXX’s location and high resistance to anaesthetic and amnestics. Each of these beings will stick to 1 of 2 distinct behaviour patterns:</p>
<ul>
<li>SCP-XXXX-1 – “Searchers”. Will search obsessively for an alleged key to SCP-XXXX when able. Can become frustrated and violent at times. Lucid and capable of conversation, highly manipulative.</li>
<li>SCP-XXXX-2 – Animalistic. Repeatedly attempts to open SCP-XXXX by force, overriding any other behavioural drives. Incapable of conversation.</li>
</ul>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> Features an extensive discovery report on the first emergence of the later-named SCP-XXXX-1, leading to discovery of XXXX and XXXX-2. Also features a report on a recurring incident with SCP-XXXX that the Foundation is still studying. References are made to a specific named researcher and her hypotheses/findings at several points to help give a connected narrative feel.<br />
Tried to give the article a progressive narrative, in that SCP-XXXX seems relatively simple at first but every new thing we learn makes it seem more and more trouble.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> As previously mentioned, progressive nature of the article meant to gradually increase intrigue.</p>
<p>An incident report states that motion sensors within cell are often tripped and cameras deactivated, only for guards to find the cell completely undisturbed and equipment behaving normally again once they get there (incident does not repeat when SCP-XXXX is under constant guard), suggesting perhaps SCP-XXXX is starting to show awareness and more physically active behaviours, or possibly just messing with electrical equipment (still being studied at “time of report”).</p>
<p>Section at end reveals that an SCP-XXXX-1 instance claimed SCP-XXXX’s area of effect would begin expanding, causing the Foundation to regularly test its size, but SCP-XXXX-1 may have been lying and no changes have yet been detected.</p>
<p>Basically, I’m trying to give the sense with both of these parts that this SCP may or may not be a ticking time bomb of sorts.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> This is my first SCP idea so I’m sure it has plenty of issues all over, so please fire away! I'm still trying to think of a better name for it.</p>
</div>
</div>
